# QA Development

- Keep modules small and surgical.
- Implement real interfaces with explicit BLOCKED behavior when providers are unconfigured.
- Expand tests/cases.json carefully; keep exactly 108 unique IDs unless the operator changes scope.
- Prefer Cal.com adapter for this repo's discovered provider; do not assume Google Calendar.
- Unit tests must prove sandbox writes cannot proceed with default settings.
- Package with scripts/create_zip.py; exclude .env and live qa evidence.
